# Release owners. Combined with the `protected-branches` ruleset's "Require review from Code Owners"
# (main and release/**), a PR that touches any of these paths needs an approving review from one of
# them. gradle.properties sets the released `version` and the `github_release` gate, and the other
# paths decide what runs, with the release credentials, when it does.
#
# There is intentionally no catch-all `*` rule: all other paths stay unowned and do NOT require these
# reviewers. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so keep the patterns below non-overlapping. Release owners are
# managed as the org team bloxbean/release-owners, which must stay visible and keep write access to this
# repository.

# This file, so the protection can't be removed without a release owner.
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @bloxbean/release-owners

# Every workflow runs with the repository's secrets once it is on a protected branch.
/.github/workflows/               @bloxbean/release-owners

# Scripts the workflows run (the BloxBean Maven repository, release-ops docs/12).
/.github/scripts/                 @bloxbean/release-owners

# Version bump -> release.
/gradle.properties                @bloxbean/release-owners

# Build logic evaluated by the credentialed release job: publication scope, signing, nmcp, and the
# Gradle distribution that runs it.
/build.gradle                     @bloxbean/release-owners
/settings.gradle                  @bloxbean/release-owners
/gradle/wrapper/                  @bloxbean/release-owners
/gradlew                          @bloxbean/release-owners
/gradlew.bat                      @bloxbean/release-owners

# The root `subprojects` block skips BOM projects, so the BOM applies nmcp and signing itself.
/zeroj-bom-core/build.gradle      @bloxbean/release-owners

# Builds the libblst natives that release.yml bundles into the published zeroj-blst jar.
/zeroj-blst/scripts/build-blst.sh @bloxbean/release-owners
